_mixer.cpp","commit_id":"c810e787114b4b6c8003e320e09fa0bce884ce79","original_commit_id":"75a9d0cecab3fc4809b63df022c4d02805796dca","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Well, actually, it's starting to feel like muting it using only Animation doesn't make much sense.\n\nFor example, muting doesn't work in cases where there are multiple AnimationPlayers, an animation from another AnimationPlayer is played via an AnimationPlaybackTrack, and that animation has an AudioTrack.\n\nThe same applies when previewing a scene in the editor using a `@tool` script outside of Animation.\n\nTherefore, wouldn't the correct implementation be to place a toggle to mute the scene somewhere above the viewport and manage it per EditorSetting or per tscn?","created_at":"2026-10-02T20:38:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T20:38:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124099#discussion_r4169635627","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124099","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godo